memmon (1.1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Restructure the repository into a proper Debian source package
    (debian/ dir, debhelper compat 13) instead of an ad hoc build
    script, so the project builds with dpkg-buildpackage and installs
    cleanly via apt.
  * Add configurable log retention: daily log files older than
    --log-retention-days (default 30, 0 disables) are deleted
    automatically. Configurable per-host via /etc/memmon/memmon.conf
    without editing the systemd unit.
  * Ship /etc/memmon/memmon.conf, sourced by the systemd unit for
    interval, log directory, and log retention.
  * Enable and start the memmon.service systemd unit automatically on
    install (handled by dh_installsystemd), so the daemon runs
    immediately after `apt install`/`apt upgrade` with no manual
    `systemctl enable --now` step required.
  * Remove committed build artifacts (compiled binary, stray .deb
    files, a redundant source zip) from version control.

 -- Shabbir Yusufali <shabyusufali@gmail.com>  Thu, 17 Sep 2026 17:58:10 +0000

